# Ubuntu 26.04 private md headers (drivers/md/)
#
# EXACT copy of the Ubuntu 26.04 kernel's drivers/md/ headers, extracted from
# linux-source-7.0.0 7.0.0-43.43 (resolute-updates).  Same vendoring rule as
# md-rhel9/, md-rhel98/ and md-vanilla/: always the target kernel's exact
# drivers/md/, never the fork's patched copy.
#
# Why stock, not the mdraid fork's 7.0 md/: Ubuntu builds md core into vmlinux
# (CONFIG_BLK_DEV_MD=y), so the fork can replace raid456/raid0/dm-raid but never
# md core itself.  The fork's md.h patches describe an md core that is not the
# one running: it makes mddev->recovery_active atomic64_t, where the running
# kernel has a 4-byte atomic_t (offset 608, padding to 616), and widens
# md_done_sync()/rdev_set_badblocks() arguments to sector_t.  raidkm must be
# compiled against what the kernel really has.
#
# Layout checked against every 7.0 flavour's vmlinux BTF (2026-11-09):
# generic 29 and 43, aws 1017, azure 1019, azure-fde 1016, gcp 1017, gke 1010,
# ibm 1018, nvidia 1025, nvidia-bos 2024, oem 1018, oracle 1016, vmware 1006:
# struct mddev 1936, md_rdev 384, bitmap_operations 272, md_done_sync 2 args,
# identical member offsets (29, nvidia, nvidia-bos and azure-fde still carry
# mddev.noio_flag in a hole; no offset moves, raidkm does not use it).
# realtime (PREEMPT_RT, 43) differs: struct mddev 2392 — NOT supported by these
# headers: tools/detect-target.sh refuses it, as it does any 7.x flavour not
# listed above (check-mddev-abi.sh fails on it; km/raid_km.c pins the layout).
#
# Files: md.h md-bitmap.h md-cluster.h raid1.h raid5.h raid10.h
